# {{name}}

A discord.py bot created with Kizuna.

## Setup

Use Python 3.11 or newer in a virtual environment.

```text
python -m pip install -e .
```

Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and set your bot token. Install the bot in a test server through the Discord Developer Portal with the `bot` and `applications.commands` scopes.

With Kizuna installed in the same environment:

```text
kizuna doctor
kizuna commands diff --guild YOUR_GUILD_ID
kizuna commands sync --guild YOUR_GUILD_ID --apply
python -m bot
```

Replace `YOUR_GUILD_ID` with your test server ID. Guild deployment copies the global definitions into that guild. To register commands globally, use `--global` instead.

Run the bot from this source checkout using the editable install. Add cogs under `src/bot/cogs/` and load them in `create_bot`. The factory must return the fully configured bot without starting it or syncing commands. This lets Kizuna inspect the same definitions used at runtime.

```text
python -m unittest discover -s tests -v
```
